WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.000
and I'd like to welcome you to this,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.200
our ninth Joy of Painting series.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.700
If this is your first time with us,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.900
I hope you drag up your paints and a big easel,

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.400
and you come and paint with us.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.960
If you've been with us before, welcome back.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.160
I'm certainly, certainly glad to see you again.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.470
So I tell you what, let's have them run all the colors

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:48.300
across the screen that you need to do this painting with me.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.250
And they'll come across in exactly the same order

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.250
as I have them on the palette,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.950
starting with a titanium white and working around.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.460
While they're doing that, let's go on up here and get started.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.960
Let me tell you what's happened already.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.000
I have an 18 by 25,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.440
24 inch canvas up here, and we've already covered it

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.090
with a nice, thin, even coat of the liquid white.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.980
The liquid white makes the canvas wet, makes it slick,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.880
it allows us to actually blend color right here

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.440
on the canvas instead of working yourself

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.140
to death on the palette.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.550
So, let's get started.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.690
We'll do a happy little painting.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.320
I thought today, tell you what,

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.700
let's do a beautiful little winter scene

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.160
that has a lot of warm colors in it.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.590
I think you'll really like it.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.080
I'm gonna take off today with a little bit of yellow ochre.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.000
Little yellow ochre, and into that a touch of bright red.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.970
and all you need is just a small amount of the red.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:37.410
It's very, very strong, very strong.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.810
Okay, let me clean my knife.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.990
Let's use, we'll use a two-inch brush.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:47.120
I'm gonna go right into this and just tap it,

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.910
very gently tap it, just get a little color on here.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.470
Let's go right back up here.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.430
Maybe we'll have a happy little sun in this painting,

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.970
so decide basically where you want the sun to be,

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.770
and I'm gonna have mine right up here.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.000
And we'll start off, and we'll just make some

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.660
some little criss-cross strokes, just like so.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:09.050
Just sort of blend it out to about like that.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:14.920
Just little criss-cross strokes, like so.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.600
There you go.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.480
Now maybe add just the smallest amount of red.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.720
I want it to be a little bit brighter

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.340
out here on the edges.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.490
We want this to be a very warm little winter scene,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.290
happy little scene.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.960
Sometimes winter scenes

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.620
Oh, they could become so cold,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.040
they're uncomfortable to look at,

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:39.590
so we'll put a little warmth in this one, just like that.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.270
Okay, now I'm gonna wash the brush.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.080
Now, we wash our brushes with odorless paint thinner,

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.730
and I really recommend you use odorless thinner,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.740
you're gonna be working by yourself.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:56.400
Shake the brush off, that's the fun part of this technique.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.000
All right, I'm gonna go right into some phthalo blue, we'll just

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.680
tap the old two-inch brush right in there,

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.200
reach right over here and grab a little bit

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.210
of the midnight black.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.320
So we have black and blue.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.640
Just mix 'em together on the brush.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.380
Let's go right back up here.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.500
Now start from the outside,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.880
'cause I want it to be darker out here

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.380
than it is up close to where the sun's gonna be.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.900
And we're still using little criss-cross strokes.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:28.260
And just begin working that right up to the color.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.000
Oh, it's a pretty little sky already.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.870
A little more color.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:39.330
Just blue and black, blue and black.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:46.200
And bring it right on around so we have sort of a vignette.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.610
Now, while we have that color in the brush,

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.830
I'm gonna have some snow down here.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.350
And in the snow, we want some shadows,

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.490
so while we have this blue and black,

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:57.790
I'm just gonna come right across here

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:00.000
and just lay in a little touch

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.180
that color.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.760
Boy, and already we have a painting ready

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.360
for the Museum of Modern Art.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:12.370
There we are, we can stop there.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.060
Okay, I'm gonna get a clean, dry two-inch brush.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.020
I have several of them here,

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.760
so I don't have to wash them all the time.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.260
And right here where these two colors come together,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:28.230
I wanna blend this so it's very soft and very gentle.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.000
There we go, be brave.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.810
Just get in here and do it, see?

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.100
Blend those edges right out.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.900
So you can't tell where one color stops

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:43.990
and the next one starts, just like so.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:44.890
And then blend outward.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.560
As your brush gets dirty, then go into the darker colors.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.780
You don't wanna take a dirty brush

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.630
and go into your light colors,

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.030
or you'll be an instant mud mixer,

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.230
then you'll be mad at me.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.670
Painting should make you happy.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.350
We stress that over and over.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.640
Really should make you happy, should make you feel good.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.230
Now, I'll wash this brush,

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:16.500
shake off the excess thinner,

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.600
and just beat the devil out of it.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.310
Okay, we said there was gonna be a sun in here.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.550
So let's use a finger, we'll finger paint today.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.290
I'm just gonna tap the old finger right on there.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:28.510
Okay, let's go up here.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.000
Decide where your sun's gonna be,

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.470
and just very firmly, very firmly,

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:39.100
rub that right in there, okay?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.400
And you can do this several times

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.390
to get any degree of lightness that you want.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:48.850
Nice bright little sun.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:51.760
Now then, if you tried just blending that,

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:53.500
chances are it would smear on you.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.420
So take your knife and very gently just go zip.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.340
Had to make that little noise or it doesn't work.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.640
Now you can blend that.

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:04.750
The value remains in the canvas.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:09.810
There we go, and we got a happy little sun.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.440
Let me tell you what, maybe there's a little cloud

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.580
that's sort of floating across there.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.800
I'll take a little black and a little blue on the fan brush.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.460
We'll use the old fan brush.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.060
You don't want much color on there, just a little.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.110
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.250
Now maybe this little cloud, he lives right up here.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:30.000
He just sort of floats around in the sky.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:34.090
Comes right across the sun there.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.930
There he comes, there he is, there he is.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.110
And this is your little cloud,

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:41.150
so wherever you want him, that's where he should be.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.550
Wherever.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.120
Clouds are one of the freest things in nature.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:50.820
They just sort of float around the sky and have a good time.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:57.090
Clean, dry brush, and this is three hairs

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:59.080
and some air, very lightly.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:06.090
very lightly, just blend this together.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.920
Isn't that fantastic?

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.930
And that easy, you have a very nice warm little sky.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:15.660
All right, now you know I lived in Alaska

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.200
for over a dozen years and I'm sort of partial to mountains,

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.930
so I think we'll put a happy little mountain in here.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.070
Now if where you live, maybe you don't have mountains

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:26.010
and you don't want a mountain in your painting,

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.550
you can certainly leave it out, that's no problem at all.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.610
Okay, I'm taking some dark sienna

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:35.130
and a little bit of the Van Dyke Brown

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:36.790
and just mixing them together.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:40.590
Okay, now pull it out very flat, very flat,

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.030
and cut across it so you have that little roll

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:45.750
of paint on the knife, it's most important.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.060
This knife has a straight edge so it's very easy to load.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.510
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:53.030
Now decide where you want the mountain to be.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:56.130
Maybe we'll have a happy little mountain

00:07:56.130 --> 00:08:00.000
that lives right there, and our mountains

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.440
They're happy, we have happy little mountains.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:06.140
There we go.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:09.590
And I'm really, really pushing this color into the canvas.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.160
Try to push it right through the fabric.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.470
Get tough with it.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:17.000
Take a strong pill.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.660
This part of the mountain goes on very firm.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.910
And all we're looking for is this nice top edge up here.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:26.450
We could care less what's happening in here.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.770
All we're looking for is a nice edge.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.930
Okay, there we go.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:35.760
That gives us a basic shape to work with.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.710
And we'll just take a two-inch brush,

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:41.880
grab this, and pull it.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:46.100
See, this canvas is wet, has the liquid white on it,

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:50.460
so you can move color.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.240
And when you're painting mountains,

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.750
if you've painted with me before,

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.830
you've certainly heard me say this over and over,

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.400
if you can see the entire mountain,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.000
the top of the mountain is always more distinct

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.560
than the bottom of the mountain.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.420
So by pulling it down and allowing it to mix

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:08.500
with the liquid white, that happens automatically.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:09.480
And I'm a lazy painter.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.100
I look for the easy way to do things.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.650
Okay, let's have some fun now.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:15.850
Let's go up here and we'll take a little bit

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:18.800
of this blue and black.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.900
And to that I'm gonna add a touch of white.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.040
Touch of white.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.090
Okay, that'll be our shadow color.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:30.000
And then we'll just use, we'll just use

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.960
some titanium white here.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.280
We'll put a little bit of snow out on the mountain.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.320
Cut across and get that small roll of paint

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.960
on the knife again, very important.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.840
Let's go right up here.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.260
All right, let's just have a little light playing

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.070
right through there.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:50.520
Now this, this is the most delicate touch imaginable.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.440
Pretend you're a whisper floating through here.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:59.800
Very gentle, very light, caress the canvas.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.620
So gentle, I get so many letters from painters

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.510
all over the country saying my snow doesn't want to break,

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:08.130
and by break I mean it has all those little holes in it.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:12.500
99 times out of 100, the problem is that you're applying

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.950
too much pressure, or you're using a paint

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:18.210
that's too soft, or a combination of both.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.760
The paint we use here is extremely firm,

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.360
and there's no pressure.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.340
No pressure at all at this stage.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.320
When you're putting the base coat of the mountain on you,

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.000
you're really strong, really pushing

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:30.850
Push it in.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:34.540
But here, just let it caress.

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:39.120
Now, a little bit of shadow color, just here and there.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.560
But notice the angles.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.270
This is going in the opposing or opposite angles.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:49.020
This is one of the simplest type of little mountains to make.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:53.100
Very easy, and it works, works so well.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.940
See here, now, maybe we wanna bring those together.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:59.600
And you can do it, can do it that easy.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.130
That easy.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:06.330
Just make all kinds of happy little things.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.460
Little ridges.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:12.200
And if you're a skier, you want to put all those

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.510
little places in so you can go and ski.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.160
Okay, that gives us a happy little mountain.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.820
Now we want to create some mist at the bottom

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.500
of this mountain, so with a clean, dry two-inch brush,

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.410
I'm going to begin tapping, being very careful

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.400
to follow the angles that are in that mountain.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:30.000
Very careful over here, we'll go in this

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.290
this direction, then lift upward,

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:37.210
still following those angles, that's most important.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.120
You can destroy your mountain here by changing the angles.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:43.350
We don't want to do that, look at that.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:46.790
That easy, we got a happy little mountain.

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:50.010
Okay, we will have a little footy hill back here.

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:54.210
And for that, I'm gonna take some black,

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:59.730
a little touch of blue, a little touch of blue, and

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.930
some white, so we have black, blue, and white.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:06.410
Maybe a little bit more of the white,

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.660
I want to lighten that up a little bit.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:11.340
About like that, good.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:14.160
Okay, let me clean my knife off,

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.250
and we'll grab the fan brush,

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.300
we'll do it with the fan brush today.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:22.170
Load it full, just really load a lot of color in there.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.610
It's black, blue, and titanium white.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.510
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.880
Decide where your little foothills live here,

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.000
and just sort of touch,

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:36.010
and begin just painting in some happy little shapes.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:38.110
Now you have to sort of make big decisions.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.620
This is your world on this piece of canvas,

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:43.120
and when you create your own world,

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.760
you have to make those decisions.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.280
Where do these little footy hills live?

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.830
They got bumps on them, they go up, down.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.960
Where are they? Where are they?

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.360
Painting gives you tremendous amounts of power

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:59.760
on this canvas, and you have to use it to make decisions.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:03.130
Okay, down there.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.770
I want to create some mist at the bottom of these.

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:15.670
So with a clean dry two-inch brush, tap like so.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.770
That creates the illusion of mist.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.870
And then come back and lift upward.

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.030
Very short little strokes,

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.570
and it'll make it look like little trees

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:28.760
way back in the distance, far, far away.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:29.670
Now, I'm gonna,

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.610
Take that same color and we're gonna add a touch

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:34.930
of alizarin crimson to it.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.780
Load the brush the same way.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.280
Just gonna add a little crimson

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.140
so it has a slight purplish hue.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:42.880
Okay, let's go back up here.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:48.160
Maybe, yep, another little row of foothills there.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.960
And you could put these on with a one-inch brush

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:53.380
or a two-inch brush, whatever, whatever.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:57.920
I just had a dirty fan brush so I thought I'd use it.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.060
Pull it down.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:04.600
Once again, we want to create that illusion of mist.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.310
So, for the two-inch brush,

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:15.150
all we're doing is just tapping, just tapping.

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:21.920
And then sometimes, you like to play some games,

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.740
and maybe make it look like there's a little light

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:25.580
playing through here.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:28.060
So I'll take just a little white on the brush,

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:30.000
and just barely touch it.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.460
right here, just, maybe there's a little light

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:35.720
playing through here, like that.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.750
Just a little bit, don't overdo, don't overdo.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:43.760
It's easy to overkill here, and then very lightly,

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:47.440
we'll just tap all that so it's very soft.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.760
See, it makes it look like there's a little bit of happy,

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.110
little sunshine playing through there on this

00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:56.450
nice cool day, there we go.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.060
Okay, now then.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:02.450
Maybe back in here there's some snow.

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.260
Let's have some fun.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:08.040
We'll go into the titanium white.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.010
Use the old fan brush.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.930
Touch of phthalo blue into that.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.530
Titanium white and phthalo blue.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.860
Phthalo blue's a beautiful blue color.

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:19.000
It's bright blue.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.310
Right up in here.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.250
Now then, here's where you begin determining

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.230
the lay of the land.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:24.990
If you've got little hills and valleys,

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:26.530
this is where you do it.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:30.000
Okay, let's go right in here and touch and make it

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:36.050
a happy little hill, right there, that easy, that easy.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:39.850
See there, and we've got a little hill.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.520
Maybe there's another hill that lives right here.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:48.510
I've just added a little more white, and that easy,

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:51.330
that easy, you can create all kinds of little hills

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:55.090
and valleys, pay particular attention

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:59.120
to the lay of the land though, look at that,

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:02.410
hill after hill.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:06.290
Now this is where I'd ski, right down here.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:09.110
I leave this up here for the experts.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.980
I fall down a lot.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:17.490
Got three left feet.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:20.910
Alright, now we need a tree.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:25.050
I'm gonna make a happy little evergreen here.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:28.350
I'm gonna take some black, some black,

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:30.000
some Prussian blue, Prussian blue.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.050
Blue is very strong, be careful with it.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.130
So we have black, Prussian blue,

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.910
we'll put some Van Dyke brown in there.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.460
Shoot, we'll even throw some Alizarin crimson in.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:45.750
You're just looking for a very dark color.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:50.110
Okay, let me clean off of it.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:53.920
And I'll just use the old fan brush.

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:56.590
Load it full of color, a lot of color.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:58.290
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.000
Now you gotta make some decisions.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.230
I think there's a tree there is now, lives right here.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.870
And use just the corner of the fan brush,

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.610
work it back and forth.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:11.270
I had a lady in class one time

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:13.510
and she called these Z trees.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:17.470
Maybe that's a good analogy, just think of making Zs.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.370
Boy, you're just like Zorro in here.

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:23.940
Look at that, those trees live right in this brush.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.840
All you have to do is sort of scare 'em out.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.030
Shake 'em a little bit.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:34.440
Like so, like so, back and forth.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.900
And you put as many or as few trees in your world

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:38.340
as you want.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:40.200
Now sometimes it's fun to play some games here.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.960
I'm gonna go to another fan brush

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:45.400
and back to that lavender color ahead.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:48.110
Back to the lavender color, okay?

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:49.410
Let's go right up in here.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:52.960
Maybe there's some trees that live far away

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.250
and as things get closer to you in the landscape,

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:56.490
they get darker in value.

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:58.800
So back here, if you wanna make the indication

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.000
of trees that live,

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.200
Just use a lighter color.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.690
See, maybe he's got a happy little friend.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.790
This right there.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:12.290
See, put as many trees or as few in your world as you want.

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.220
It's up to you.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:16.700
Just want to show you how to make a tree,

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:19.900
and you decide how many trees live in your world.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.180
Maybe, let's do it over here too.

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:24.180
I want some trees on this side.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:28.030
While we have this lavender looking color going.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.770
Just drop in an indication of a happy little tree there.

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:43.640
And there, there we go, all right.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.470
Now we go back to our brush, it has a dark color.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:52.510
And, yep, I'm gonna put a tree.

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:56.160
Now this old tree, when he was just a little baby,

00:18:56.160 --> 00:19:00.000
maybe a big deer came by and stepped on him

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:07.170
Hurt him a little bit, so he's sort of bent.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:10.520
I think, personally, landscapes look better

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.360
if all the trees aren't perfectly straight.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.230
Terrible to think that every tree

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:17.740
is just a future telephone pole.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.040
Put some shape in your trees.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:23.910
Let 'em bend and just have fun.

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:35.450
Right on down.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.590
Now this could be done with a two-inch brush,

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:43.890
or a one-inch brush works very nicely also, no problem.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:49.790
Okay, a little tree right there.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.380
I like to do these evergreen trees.

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:54.460
In my home in Alaska, there was a lot of evergreens.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.680
I had one in my front yard that,

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:59.410
gosh, it must have been 60, 70 feet tall.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.020
and the ptarmigan used to set up there.

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:04.400
Ptarmigan's a beautiful bird in the wintertime,

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:09.230
he turns white, and he's so pretty, so pretty.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:12.340
I think he's in the grouse family.

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:13.830
Beautiful bird.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.350
Alaska's the only place I've ever seen him,

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:19.980
but I'm sure there are other places.

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:28.190
Nothing that pretty could be just in one place.

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:30.000
Dark color, we're looking for contrast.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:35.990
Let's put one right here too, what the heck.

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:39.070
What the heck.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.200
This will give you a lot of practice making

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.890
some happy little evergreens.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:50.400
There we are.

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:52.400
And down in here, you could cure less.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.860
You separate these with highlights.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:55.940
We're gonna come back and highlight this some.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.860
So right now, all we're looking for is color.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.000
Just want color on here.

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:05.720
That's all.

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:09.590
All right, now then, we need some trunks in there

00:21:09.590 --> 00:21:10.790
to hold up these little trees.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:13.240
So I'll use some of the dark sienna,

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:16.510
a little bit of white,

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:18.790
cut us off a tiny little roll of paint.

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:23.530
Let's go back up here, right up through here,

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:25.600
and just touch here and there.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:27.360
You're not gonna see the entire trunk,

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:28.700
you're just gonna see parts of it,

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:29.700
so don't worry about it.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:34.810
Just enjoy, there.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.430
And sometimes you can see the indication

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:43.420
of little trunks that are hid back in there.

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:45.900
Okay, let's go on the other side over here.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:49.600
We don't want these little trees to be left out.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:55.000
They get upset if you don't give them a trunk too.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.380
Don't want his feelings hurt.

00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:59.060
These are happy little trees.

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.000
They can take just the point

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:03.400
and scratch in a few little dead limbs.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:06.920
Evergreens always have dead limbs on 'em.

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:09.460
Okay, I'm gonna go right into some liquid white

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:12.400
'cause I'm looking for a paint that's a little thinner.

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:20.190
Titanium white, and a little bit of phthalo blue, okay?

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:22.180
Now then, let's put some highlight.

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:23.540
Here's your light source.

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:26.190
So over here, the left side of the tree

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:29.320
is gonna be brighter than the right side.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:30.000
Just drop in some light.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.160
some highlights, like so.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:34.950
Darker, darker, darker as it goes down.

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:38.460
Now this is a thinner paint, so it sticks on top of here

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:40.020
without any problem.

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:44.400
If your paint won't stick, make it a little bit thinner,

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:48.600
and then you'll find it works better.

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.960
One of our golden rules, if this is your first time with us,

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:54.490
is that a thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:57.730
So we start off with the thickest paint we can find,

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.000
and then each layer gets thinner, and that's

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.060
what makes all this work, there's no big secret to it.

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:07.770
There we go, just an indication

00:23:07.770 --> 00:23:09.780
of a few little highlights here and there.

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:13.310
Darker, darker, darker.

00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:18.190
There it is, and then it gets down in here,

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:23.990
more shadows, darker and darker and darker.

00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:27.110
Okay, here's the old paintbrush.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:34.830
right into some white, a little bit of the blue.

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:39.360
Let's start right in here

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:41.930
and we'll put another happy little hill.

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:43.610
It's allowed to pick up some of this dark color

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:45.900
and that becomes shadows.

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:49.270
See there, that easy.

00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:52.540
And create your shadows all at once.

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.950
Okay, now maybe there's some little grassy things

00:23:54.950 --> 00:23:57.060
that grow right in there, there they are.

00:23:57.060 --> 00:23:58.380
You can just push them in.

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:03.850
Like so, see?

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:06.730
Now then, now then.

00:24:06.730 --> 00:24:08.770
Over here, let's go right over on this side.

00:24:08.770 --> 00:24:10.830
Here's another little plane.

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:12.190
So each one of these little hills you make

00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:14.530
creates a different plane in your painting

00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:16.520
and helps, it really helps create

00:24:16.520 --> 00:24:19.040
the illusion of depth and distance.

00:24:19.040 --> 00:24:22.380
There we go.

00:24:22.380 --> 00:24:25.230
And once again, let it pick up some of this dark color

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:28.550
and pull it down.

00:24:28.550 --> 00:24:30.000
Follow the lay of the land.

00:24:31.560 --> 00:24:35.370
very important at this time, very important.

00:24:35.370 --> 00:24:39.890
Okay, I'll add a little touch of the liquid white,

00:24:39.890 --> 00:24:42.130
and that thinner paint, once again, see,

00:24:42.130 --> 00:24:43.830
I can pull that up and make all kinds

00:24:43.830 --> 00:24:45.850
of happy little things happen.

00:24:45.850 --> 00:24:50.160
Here I'm just pushing upward, give it a little upward pull,

00:24:50.160 --> 00:24:57.970
just make all kinds of pretty things.

00:24:57.970 --> 00:24:59.830
I like these little winter scenes.

00:25:01.530 --> 00:25:03.270
Now I'm just sort of working back and forth

00:25:03.270 --> 00:25:07.480
with the blues and the whites.

00:25:07.480 --> 00:25:11.790
Tell you what, if you've painted with me before,

00:25:11.790 --> 00:25:13.470
you know I'm a water fanatic.

00:25:13.470 --> 00:25:15.420
So let's have some water in this.

00:25:15.420 --> 00:25:16.960
I like water.

00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:18.340
So I'm just gonna tap the brush

00:25:18.340 --> 00:25:24.510
into a tiny bit of the phthalo blue, black.

00:25:24.510 --> 00:25:25.960
Okay, let's go right back up here.

00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:28.360
Make a decision, water lives right here.

00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:29.920
There it is, there it is.

00:25:30.190 --> 00:25:32.860
That easy, that easy.

00:25:32.860 --> 00:25:36.480
Just pull it down, straight down.

00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:38.670
Be sure these lines come straight down.

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:41.250
And then very lightly go across.

00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:43.510
And that'll create the illusion of water.

00:25:43.510 --> 00:25:44.850
That easy, maybe we'll take it right off

00:25:44.850 --> 00:25:47.400
the end of the canvas, there you go.

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:51.520
That's just a happy little pond that lives out there.

00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:55.210
Then we'll take a little bit of this dark color.

00:25:55.210 --> 00:25:57.650
Maybe there's a stone right here.

00:25:57.650 --> 00:25:59.160
So we'll put the stone on.

00:26:01.690 --> 00:26:05.500
There lives a little stone right there.

00:26:05.500 --> 00:26:09.060
He's got a little friend named Harold.

00:26:09.060 --> 00:26:13.690
This is Harold the Stone right here.

00:26:13.690 --> 00:26:16.700
Flecked a little bit of that down in here.

00:26:16.700 --> 00:26:21.100
Take our two-inch brush, pull that down, come across.

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:25.590
Now then, our fan brush that has the white on it.

00:26:25.590 --> 00:26:27.570
And as I say, I have several of each brush going here

00:26:27.570 --> 00:26:29.600
so I don't have to wash them between each time.

00:26:31.560 --> 00:26:35.590
Let's put a little bit of snow right up on that rock.

00:26:35.590 --> 00:26:37.700
It's that easy.

00:26:37.700 --> 00:26:50.550
Some liquid white on the knife,

00:26:50.550 --> 00:26:53.230
pull it out very flat, cross it,

00:26:53.230 --> 00:26:55.590
and we just put a little water line,

00:26:55.590 --> 00:27:00.000
a little bit of snow laying right here, just like so.

00:27:04.990 --> 00:27:08.510
Isn't that a nice little snow scene?

00:27:08.510 --> 00:27:10.290
And it's easy, you can do it.

00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:13.520
Little bit of snow laying right out through there.

00:27:13.520 --> 00:27:15.960
I think we have a painting that's ready for a signature.

00:27:15.960 --> 00:27:17.140
I'm gonna dip my brush right into

00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:19.630
a little bit of the liquid clear,

00:27:19.630 --> 00:27:20.890
bring it to a nice sharp point,

00:27:20.890 --> 00:27:22.680
and we'll sign it right here.

00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:24.260
I hope you've enjoyed this painting.

00:27:24.260 --> 00:27:26.160
It's a lot of fun,

00:27:26.160 --> 00:27:30.000
and I look forward to seeing you again next time.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:33.050
To all of us here, I'd like to wish you happy painting.

00:27:33.050 --> 00:27:33.810
God bless.
